# Commercial S11.2-R15.14 Gate error loss diagnosis

Date: 2026-09-27
Scope: Source-only diagnosis; no runtime mutation

## Observed result

The single authorised R15.13 runtime attempt stopped before any Technical
probe, S11 installation or Canary start. The controller exposed only
`S11_2_TECHNICAL_GATE_READ_RED`; the Gate output available to the controller
contained only the Python exception type `ValueError`.

## First information-loss location

`scripts/tu1nz_adult_public_s11_2_gate.py` caught `ValueError` and serialized
`type(error).__name__`. A canonical error such as
`S11_2_TECHNICAL_BINDING_MISSING` therefore became `ValueError`. Arbitrary
exception text was not exposed, but the actionable safe code was destroyed.

## Second information-loss location

`write_technical_profile()` in
`scripts/tu1nz_adult_public_s11_2_control.sh` redirected Gate stdout to a file
and used a generic shell failure branch. Any non-zero Gate exit became only
`S11_2_TECHNICAL_GATE_READ_RED`; the Gate envelope, component, classification
and exit status were not validated or preserved.

## Correction boundary

R15.14 adds one exact allowlist, `GATE_FAILURE_V1`, and
`GATE_DIAGNOSTIC_V1`. Unknown/free-form `ValueError` text and database, OS or
JSON detail are mapped to bounded codes. The controller validates size, JSON
shape, schema, version, child allowlist, taxonomy and exit consistency before
preserving stable outer context plus exact safe inner cause. A non-zero Gate
still stops before probes, S11 and Canary. No runtime deployment or retry is
part of this correction.
